    { math: '1 · Nebula → protostar', note: 'Gravity gathers a cold cloud of gas and dust; compression heats the core. Ten million years for a Sun-mass cloud to reach ignition.' },
    { math: '2 · Main sequence (hydrogen burning)', note: 'Fusion of hydrogen into helium — the longest, most stable stage. The Sun: ~10 billion years, currently halfway. A star\'s mass sets everything: heavier = hotter, brighter, shorter-lived.' },
